ff802-cc
========

Manual USB mode switch for the original RME Fireface 802 (not the 802 FS).

  sudo ff802-cc check     read only: is a unit in proprietary mode there,
                          do its USB descriptors match? Sends nothing.
  sudo ff802-cc enable    proprietary (2a39:3fcd) -> class-compliant
                          (0424:3fdd): sends 01 00 44 BD to interface 1,
                          bulk OUT 0x0C, then resets the USB hub port of
                          the unit (sysfs disable=1, 2 s, disable=0) and
                          waits for 0424:3fdd
  sudo ff802-cc --no-port-reset enable
                          the same without the port reset: disconnect and
                          reconnect the unit by hand afterwards
  sudo ff802-cc disable   class-compliant -> proprietary: sends 16 bytes
                          to USB-MIDI interface 3, bulk OUT 0x07 (libusb
                          detaches snd-usb-audio from that interface; the
                          ALSA card disappears), waits for 2a39:3fcd
  ff802-detect            lists the unit and its mode (never opens it)

Every switch shows the target and the bytes and needs the typed word
ENABLE or DISABLE on an interactive terminal. Nothing is ever retried.
Both directions were tested on the device on 2026-11-19.

Safety and preconditions
------------------------

- Root is needed (sudo): for the USB device node and, for enable, for
  the hub port. No udev rule or polkit rule is installed.
- enable resolves the hub port before anything is sent; it must be the
  port of exactly this unit, otherwise nothing is sent.
- disable refuses while the automation of ff802-cc-auto is on (it would
  switch the unit straight back): run "ff802-cc-auto off" first. It also
  refuses while audio is playing or recording on the unit.
- Volume: after enable the unit appears as an audio device; with
  ff802-cc-auto/ff802-ucm-profile its six outputs come back with the
  volumes stored by WirePlumber.

Exit status: 0 switched (or check passed), 1 no suitable unit, 2 usage,
3 precondition failed (nothing sent), 4 transfer failed (unit state
unknown), 5 not sent (aborted), 6 transferred, new mode not detected.

Versions
--------

  ff802-cc --version       (example)
  ff802-cc 0.5.0 (git <revision>, Release, USB writes enabled)

- Project version (0.5.0): version of the fireface802-cc sources, set in
  CMakeLists.txt; shown by --version of all programs.
- Git revision (12 hex digits): the commit the programs were built from,
  determined by CMake at configure time.
- Package version (changelog of this package, 0.5.0 here): version
  of the Debian package ff802-cc. It may differ from the project version,
  e.g. 0.5.0-2 for a package-only change, or 0.5.1 built for an upgrade
  test.
- /usr/share/doc/ff802-cc/BUILDINFO: commit, build type, compiler, CMake
  and libusb versions and SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH of the build. The package is
  built reproducibly: the same commit built with the same tool versions
  gives the same .deb.

Relation to the other packages
------------------------------

Independent: ff802-cc needs neither ff802-cc-auto nor ff802-ucm-profile,
and they do not need it. Files of the three packages do not overlap.
ff802-cc only reads the automation state /var/lib/ff802-cc-auto/mode
(missing = off).

Removal
-------

  sudo apt remove ff802-cc     (no configuration, nothing left behind)
